  "footnote": "Twelve distinct courses totaling at least 36 credits: nine STS courses and three science courses. Every major course must be at least 3 credits, letter graded C- or higher. Independent study credits do not count toward the major, including STS 3991. Admission requires successful completion of one non-FWS STS course and an application normally submitted in sophomore year; juniors are considered case by case. The application includes a one-page statement of intellectual interests and a tentative course plan. Complete BIO-AS, PHS-AS, SDS-AS and SMR-AS distributions early to prepare for further science courses. Optional honors requires a 3.00 overall Cornell GPA, a 3.30 major GPA, a research topic, a supervisor and a second faculty advisor (at least one in STS), with entry considered at the end of junior spring; honors adds no checklist rows.",
